This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1]: Since the ya have the unID'd appearance as "bamboo arrow",
shouldn't their symbol be the brown, for the wood items, instead of the
metally cyan? Yes, they should. --Chilliwack

[2]: The effects of light sources (not just candles) should be
cumulative. i.e. if you have three lit lamps, you should be able to see
further than if you have fewer. --rogza

[3]: When asked what kind of scroll one wants to write with a magic
marker, if answered "Elbereth", the game should give you a ?oSM
--HanClinto

[4]: If you're in a pit, you should be able to dig into an adjacent
(non-wall) square and create another pit, without having to climb out
first. If that square has a boulder, the pit would then be immediately
filled. --BenUrban

[5]: One should be able to move directly from one pit to an adjacent
pit (treating non-pit squares as walls) freely, without having to climb
out or fall in. --BenUrban

[6]: YAFM when entering a used armor store: "This shop reminds you of a
locker room" --Botje

[7]: some small penalty for cavemen breaking illiterate conduct or
using certain 'complex' tools --teabing

[8]: New conduct "never wore clothing" and subsets "never wore body
armour" --Yui

[9]: Throwing a cloak, towel, robe, or similar at an enemy
(close-range) should have a chance of blinding it temporarily. --JoshJ

[10]: (a)pplying a stethoscope to a door should allow you to hear
what's on the other side (such as shops or special rooms). --JoshJ

[11]: Candy Bars should give you a ten turn speed boost --Cheapy|

[12]: When a pit is generated, have it generate if it is poisoned or
not, so the status does not change later. --Hours_

[13]: Sinks in the same room as an altar should have a (tiny) chance of
providing (un)holy water --Botje

[14]: There should always be a guaranteed random instrument available
before arriving at the castle. --aristotle73

[15]: Using a scroll of enchant weapon while wielding an iron chain
should produce a chain whip. It should be similar to a bullwhip, but
deal better damage (and actually hurt thick-skinned monsters).
--NE[S]outlaw

Individual ideas may have contributions from multiple authors/editors,
but we currently only record the nickname of (usually) the original
